{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > prepare_order_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind='code_observation') for i,f,a,b in [('src_inmem_constructor','inmem_transport.go',40,103),('src_newraft_initial','api.go',496,625),('src_rpc_dispatch','raft.go',1390,1413),('src_request_fields','commands.go',6,65),('src_mock_fsm','testing.go',34,105)]]\ng=dict(source_ids=['src_pipeline_match','src_inmem_pipeline','src_future_completion','src_pipeline_send'],expectation_ids=['src_pipeline_interface'],binding_ids=['bind_pipeline_response'],derivation='Observe the actual pipelineDecode call through a forwarding AppendFuture wrapper. Error records return only after delegating to the real completed future. First Response entry records whether Error already returned. The property is response_accessed implies error_returned_before_response, never an equality between response success and RPC success.',applicability='Two isolated decoder operations receive independently produced real in-memory futures: a timeout with an unserviced receiver, and a successful empty append processed by a real NewRaft follower. Consumer completion and stable operation identity are recorded separately from the result.',alternatives=['The real transport publishes after completion, protecting write visibility; this does not perform the required Error invocation.','Timeout response remains zero-valued and does not advance match support.'],unresolved=['Network pipeline branch is not executed.','No leader election prefix, log commitment or application consequence is exercised.'])\nlegality=dict(source_ids=['src_inmem_constructor','src_inmem_pipeline','src_newraft_initial','src_rpc_dispatch','src_append_producer','src_request_fields','src_mock_fsm','src_pipeline_match'],expectation_ids=['src_pipeline_interface'],derivation='Use actual in-memory transport request enqueue, completion decoder, and per-request future identity. A connected receiver without a worker yields the transport own timeout. Successful cases create an unbootstrapped empty follower through NewRaft using empty real in-memory stores, then send a protocol-version-matched empty term-1 AppendEntries request with no predecessor or commit index. The real worker produces its reply. This is a local RPC/consumer contract input, not an elected-leader history. pipelineDecode is invoked with minimal peer and notification state; empty entries cannot reach commitment.match. No target logic is replaced.',applicability='Method ordering before response interpretation requires no quorum, elected leadership, log entry, or FSM action. The isolated consumer has no concurrent writers. Receiver workers stay live through successful reply; timeout case omits receiver processing as its declared delay fault. Consumer stop is supplied after response entry or natural decoder termination, and completion is awaited before result observation.',alternatives=['A full cluster history would be needed for a claim about decision safety but does not determine this interface method order.'],unresolved=['The harness does not establish the synthetic sender as a legally elected leader; this is excluded from the local claim.','The network transport and configuration transitions remain outside this execution.'])\nplan=dict(description='Measure same-future Error-return-before-Response in the real pipeline decoder, with real built-in completion producers and an independent permitted-order control.',claim_id='O_pipeline_response_order',binding_ids=['bind_pipeline_response'],harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='TestAssurancePipelineResponseOrder runs decoder_timeout, decoder_success, and permitted_control. The first two call actual pipelineDecode; the last explicitly follows the interface ordering and is an unmonitored observation control. Every request is paired with its exact returned and consumed future. order_admitted is emitted after production but before decoder delivery. order_result is emitted after decoder completion. Auxiliary raw response fields are read from the original response storage, not treated as valid successful results when Error is nonnil.',semantic_changes=['A forwarding future wrapper records only Error return and first Response invocation; it delegates original values and does not pre-call Error.','A pipeline proxy delivers that same wrapped real future to an isolated real decoder; transport producer output is otherwise unchanged.','The decoder receiver and followerReplication are minimally initialized; no leadership prefix is claimed. Empty requests exclude match-index and application effects.','Timeout is generated by actual InmemTransport; tool timeouts call t.Fatal and do not emit a completed comparison.','The permitted control uses a separate operation and future; it never supplies history for either decoder case.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='admission',event='order_admitted',conditions=[dict(field='consumer',op='ne',value='permitted_control'),dict(field='same_future',op='eq',value=True)])],legality=legality),monitors=[dict(id='monitor_pipeline_order',checker_id='check_pipeline_order',event='order_result',binding_ids=['bind_pipeline_response'],grounding=g,admission_alias='admission',applicability_conditions=[dict(field='consumer',op='ne',value='permitted_control')])],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='check_pipeline_order',kind='event_implication',trigger=dict(field='completed',op='eq',value=True),antecedent=dict(field='response_accessed',op='eq',value=True),assertion=dict(field='error_returned_before_response',op='eq',value=True),identity_fields=['operation'],description='For each completed decoder operation, if Response was accessed on its admitted future then Error must already have returned on that same future.')],uncertainties=['Only the in-memory producer is executed; network producer support is sourced but not execution coverage.','A contract mismatch does not establish use of invalid successful support: the timeout response remains false and the successful reply comes from the actual follower.','The unbootstrapped follower and supplied term-1 request are an RPC prefix for this local interface check, not a proven election history.'])\njson.dump(plan,open('pipeline-order-plan.json','w'),indent=2)\nsub=dict(action='check',unit_id='unit-O_pipeline_response_order',plan_path='pipeline-order-plan.json',harness_path='pipeline_order_test.go',files={},sources=sources,rationale='Execute the accepted local access-order obligation using real in-memory pipeline completion and actual pipelineDecode. A forwarding wrapper measures calls without substituting a response or altering target behavior. Include actual timeout and successful follower reply, plus an independent permitted-order control. Record completed consumer results separately from admission; do not infer consensus safety or liveness from either response or tool status.')\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-order-check.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 prepare_order_check.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(json.load(open('submission-order-check.json')),json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')))\np=json.load(open('pipeline-order-plan.json')); p['harness']['source']=open('pipeline_order_test.go').read()\njsonschema.validate(p,json.load(open('../product-schemas.json'))['DirectCheckPlan'])\nprint('Submission and plan (with captured harness bytes) validate.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
